[MEDIUM] SECRET_KEY env var is ignored
  Recipe:   Set SECRET_KEY=mysecret in the environment and restart the server. Mint a cookie with server.make_session_cookie(uid) using a fresh app, restart with the SAME env, and verify the old cookie still works. Today it does NOT — server reads data/secret.key on every call and the env var has no effect.
  Evidence: server.py:_get_secret_key() reads SECRET_FILE (data/secret.key) and never consults os.environ['SECRET_KEY']. Verified by setting SECRET_KEY and inspecting data/secret.key — env value not present. Migrations between hosts will invalidate sessions.

[MEDIUM] No CSRF token; protection relies solely on SameSite=Lax cookie attribute
  Recipe:   Open a logged-in tab to http://127.0.0.1:8080. From another origin (e.g. file:// or http://localhost:9999) submit a form/JS POST to http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/state. Without SameSite=Strict, top-level cross-origin POSTs still include the cookie in older browsers, and a determined attacker can use a same-site subdomain bypass. Mitigation: also require a CSRF token in body for state writes.
  Evidence: server.py:_set_session_cookie sets SameSite='Lax' but no token. State-mutating endpoints (PUT /api/state, POST /api/auth/logout) accept any same-site request as long as the cookie is present. Top-level GET navigations include Lax cookies but cannot mutate state.

[HIGH] MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH=64KB is effectively dead code: real limit is ~256KB and is masked as 400 JSON error
  Recipe:   PUT /api/state with a real-HTTP body > 64KB (use make_server + urllib; test_client alone masks this). Real limit observed: ~256KB parsed re-encode. 5MB returns 400 '请求体不是合法的 JSON' instead of 413.
  Evidence: Real-HTTP test (make_server + urllib):
  64KB+1 body -> 200
  100KB body -> 200
  300KB body -> 200
  500KB body -> 200
  1MB body -> 200 (first) / 409 (repeat OCC)
  5MB body -> 400 '请求体不是合法的 JSON'
_json_body()'s `except Exception` catches RequestEntityTooLarge and returns 400 instead of letting the 413 handler fire.

